IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa4-general-duties`
IMPORT `coa4-declaration`
IMPORT `coa4-approval-loans`
IMPORT `coa5-loans-exceptions`

-- coa-proc-director-interests.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), a director's interest in a transaction and loans to directors:
-- ss 177 (declaration of a proposed transaction), 182 to 184 (declaration after the company has entered into it), 197 (loans: the members' approval),
-- 204 and 207 (the two exceptions taken as gates), 213 and 214 (a loan in contravention: avoidance, the account and indemnity, affirmation).
-- Lines 2364-2380, 2413-2445, 2570-2587, 2687-2696, 2729-2737 and 2796-2821 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
-- This is the procedure the Act lays down, written as regulative rules over the Boolean encoding in coa4-general-duties.l4, coa4-declaration.l4,
-- coa4-approval-loans.l4 and coa5-loans-exceptions.l4. Those modules hold the gates and they are CALLED here; nothing in them is edited, and
-- the two regulative rules they already hold for s 177 and s 182 are neither called nor changed (see notes/procedure-coa-proc-director-interests.md).
--
-- SEAMS taken as INPUTS: whether the director is aware (ss 177(5), 182(5)); whether the interest need not be declared (ss 177(6), 182(6)); the day the
-- company enters into the transaction; the last day on which a declaration is still "as soon as is reasonably practicable" (a judgment, the Act
-- gives no number); the last day of "a reasonable period" for an affirmation (the same); that a resolution of the members was passed; the answers of
-- the Boolean functions for ss 197(2), 213(1), 213(4), 213(6), 213(7) and 214, each computed by the caller.
-- NOT ENCODED as regulative rules: s 184(5) (a deeming rule: no person is bound and no time runs; it stays Boolean in coa4-declaration.l4),
-- s 182(3) and s 183(2) (a further declaration after entry; the penalty), s 197(2)'s separate approval beyond the answer taken as an input to the s 197(1) rule,
-- ss 205, 206, 208, 209 (the other exceptions; one input says whether any of them applies), and the amounts of ss 213(3)(a) and (b) (Boolean already).

DECLARE `ss 177-214 party` IS ONE OF
    `ss 177-214 the director`
    `ss 177-214 the company`
    `ss 177-214 the members of the company`
    `ss 177-214 a person liable under section 213(4)`

DECLARE `ss 177-214 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 177(1) the director declares the nature and extent of the interest to the other directors`
    `s 177(3) the director makes a further declaration to the other directors`
    `s 182(2)(a) the director declares at a meeting of the directors`
    `s 182(2)(b) the director declares by notice in writing`
    `s 182(2)(c) the director declares by general notice`
    `s 197(1) the company makes the loan or gives the guarantee or provides the security`
    `s 197(3) the members pass the resolution approving the transaction`
    `s 213(2) the company avoids the transaction or arrangement`
    `s 213(3)(a) the person accounts to the company for the gain`
    `s 213(3)(b) the person indemnifies the company for the loss or damage`
    `s 214 the members of the company affirm the transaction or arrangement by resolution`

-- ---- s 177: declaration of a proposed transaction, before the company enters into it ------------------------------------------------

-- The helpers turn the two dates into the number of days the DEONTIC needs. The Act's limit is an event ("before the company enters into the transaction"),
-- so it is counted from two dates the caller supplies and never written as a literal.
-- src:2372 | (4) Any declaration required by this section must be made before the company enters into the transaction or arrangement.
@ref s 177(4) Any declaration required by this section must be made before the company enters into the transaction or arrangement (src:2372)
-- FORK: s 177(4) "before the company enters into the transaction" | a declaration on the day of entry, before the company enters into it that day, is in time, so the last day is the day of entry (the usual case is a declaration at the board meeting that approves the transaction, with entry later that day); a day-granular clock cannot tell before from after within a day, and this reading does not resolve that against the director (src:2372) | a declaration must be made on a day earlier than the day of entry, so the last day is the day before it (the encoder's first reading, changed after independent review)
-- FORK: s 177(1) "proposed transaction" | s 177 applies only while the company has not yet entered into the transaction, so the rule needs the day of entry to be later than day 0, and where it is not the rule gives no duty (s 182 then governs) | the duty has arisen and has already been breached
GIVEN dayZero IS A DATE
      dayOfEntry IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 177(4) the company has not yet entered into the transaction on the day the duty to declare arises` MEANS
    (Day dayOfEntry) GREATER THAN (Day dayZero)

GIVEN dayZero IS A DATE
      dayOfEntry IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 177(4) the last day for the declaration, counted from day 0` MEANS
    (Day dayOfEntry) MINUS (Day dayZero)

-- src:2364 | 177 Duty to declare interest in proposed transaction or arrangement
-- src:2365 | (1) If a director of a company is in any way, directly or indirectly, interested in a proposed transaction or arrangement with the company, he must declare the nature and extent of that interest to the other directors.
-- src:2372 | (4) Any declaration required by this section must be made before the company enters into the transaction or arrangement.
@ref s 177(1) and (4) Duty to declare interest in proposed transaction or arrangement (src:2364-2365 and src:2372)
-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the director's duty to declare arises (the director is interested in the proposed transaction and aware of it, s 177(5)); counting="before the company enters into the transaction or arrangement" (the last day is the day of entry itself, see the FORK above)
-- Gate: s 177(1) with the answers under s 177(5) and s 177(6). Where the gate does not answer JUST TRUE (not aware, need not declare, or not known) there is no duty and the rule is FULFILLED.
-- s 177(2) says the declaration "may (but need not)" be made at a meeting or by notice, so the manner does not matter and there is one act.
GIVEN `the director is in any way, directly or indirectly, interested in a proposed transaction or arrangement with the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer under section 177(5)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under section 177(6)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      dayZero IS A DATE
      dayOfEntry IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ss 177-214 party` `ss 177-214 act`
`s 177(1) and (4) the director's duty to declare before the company enters into the transaction` MEANS
    IF     (`s 177(1) the director is obliged to declare the nature and extent of the interest to the other directors` `the director is in any way, directly or indirectly, interested in a proposed transaction or arrangement with the company` `the answer under section 177(5)` `the answer under section 177(6)`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND (`s 177(4) the company has not yet entered into the transaction on the day the duty to declare arises` dayZero dayOfEntry)
    THEN PARTY `ss 177-214 the director`
         MUST `s 177(1) the director declares the nature and extent of the interest to the other directors`
         WITHIN (`s 177(4) the last day for the declaration, counted from day 0` dayZero dayOfEntry)
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `ss 177-214 the director` BECAUSE "the director did not declare the nature and extent of the interest to the other directors before the company entered into the transaction or arrangement (s 177(1) and (4)); no offence is stated for s 177 and its consequences are those of the general duties (s 178)"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:2371 | (3) If a declaration of interest under this section proves to be, or becomes, inaccurate or incomplete, a further declaration must be made.
-- src:2372 | (4) Any declaration required by this section must be made before the company enters into the transaction or arrangement.
@ref s 177(3) and (4) A further declaration (src:2371 and src:2372)
-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the declaration proves to be, or becomes, inaccurate or incomplete; counting="before the company enters into the transaction or arrangement" (s 177(4) says "any declaration required by this section", so the same limit applies to the further declaration)
-- FORK: s 177(3) "proves to be, or becomes, inaccurate or incomplete" | a further declaration is owed no later than the day of entry, as s 177(4) says of any declaration required by the section; where the declaration becomes inaccurate only after entry the rule gives no duty and s 182 governs | the further declaration may be made after entry
GIVEN `a declaration of interest under section 177 proves to be, or becomes, inaccurate or incomplete` IS A BOOLEAN
      dayZero IS A DATE
      dayOfEntry IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ss 177-214 party` `ss 177-214 act`
`s 177(3) and (4) the director's duty to make a further declaration before the company enters into the transaction` MEANS
    IF     (`s 177(3) a further declaration must be made` `a declaration of interest under section 177 proves to be, or becomes, inaccurate or incomplete`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND (`s 177(4) the company has not yet entered into the transaction on the day the duty to declare arises` dayZero dayOfEntry)
    THEN PARTY `ss 177-214 the director`
         MUST `s 177(3) the director makes a further declaration to the other directors`
         WITHIN (`s 177(4) the last day for the declaration, counted from day 0` dayZero dayOfEntry)
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `ss 177-214 the director` BECAUSE "the director did not make the further declaration before the company entered into the transaction or arrangement (s 177(3) and (4))"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- ---- ss 182 to 184: declaration of an interest in a transaction the company has entered into ------------------------------------------

-- "As soon as is reasonably practicable" is a standard and not a number. The last day on which a declaration still meets it is a judgment of the caller (a seam),
-- counted from day 0 by the helper; a last day earlier than day 0 is read as day 0 itself.
-- src:2421 | (4) Any declaration required by this section must be made as soon as is reasonably practicable.
@ref s 182(4) As soon as is reasonably practicable (src:2421)
-- FORK: s 182(4) "as soon as is reasonably practicable" | the caller states the last day on which a declaration is still as soon as is reasonably practicable, and the declaration is in time up to and including that day | the Act's own words give no day, so the rule has no clock
GIVEN dayZero IS A DATE
      lastDay IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 182(4) the days allowed, counted from day 0` MEANS
    IF (Day lastDay) AT LEAST (Day dayZero)
    THEN (Day lastDay) MINUS (Day dayZero)
    ELSE 0

-- src:2413 | 182 Declaration of interest in existing transaction or arrangement
-- src:2414 | (1) Where a director of a company is in any way, directly or indirectly, interested in a transaction or arrangement that has been entered into by the company, he must declare the nature and extent of the interest to the other directors in accordance with this section.
-- src:2415 | This section does not apply if or to the extent that the interest has been declared under section 177 (duty to declare interest in proposed transaction or arrangement).
-- src:2416 | (2) The declaration must be made—
-- src:2417 | (a) at a meeting of the directors, or
-- src:2418 | (b) by notice in writing (see section 184), or
-- src:2419 | (c) by general notice (see section 185).
-- src:2421 | (4) Any declaration required by this section must be made as soon as is reasonably practicable.
-- src:2431 | 183 Offence of failure to declare interest
-- src:2432 | (1) A director who fails to comply with the requirements of section 182 (declaration of interest in existing transaction or arrangement) commits an offence.
@ref s 182(1), (2) and (4), and s 183(1) The duty to declare as soon as is reasonably practicable, and the offence (src:2413-2419 and src:2421 and src:2431-2432)
-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the director's duty to declare arises (the company has entered into the transaction and the director is, or is treated as, aware of the interest and of the transaction, s 182(5)); counting="as soon as is reasonably practicable" (the Act gives no number: the last day is a date the caller supplies as a judgment, and a declaration on that day is in time)
-- s 182(2) says the declaration "must be made" at a meeting, by notice in writing or by general notice, so the three ways are alternatives (ROR) and each one is a way the Act allows; s 177(2) differs, see above.
-- The breach is the failure that s 183(1) makes an offence ("a director who fails to comply with the requirements of section 182 commits an offence"). The penalty of s 183(2) stays Boolean in coa4-declaration.l4.
-- FORK: s 183(1) "fails to comply with the requirements of section 182" | the offence is encoded as the BREACH of this rule (the time requirement of s 182(4)), and the unbreached underlying duty is the next rule | the offence is committed only if the declaration is never made
GIVEN `the director is in any way, directly or indirectly, interested in a transaction or arrangement that has been entered into by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interest has been declared under section 177` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer under section 182(5)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under section 182(6)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      dayZero IS A DATE
      lastDay IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ss 177-214 party` `ss 177-214 act`
`s 182(4) and s 183(1) the director's duty to declare as soon as is reasonably practicable` MEANS
    IF (`s 182(1) the director is obliged to declare the nature and extent of the interest to the other directors` `the director is in any way, directly or indirectly, interested in a transaction or arrangement that has been entered into by the company` `the interest has been declared under section 177` `the answer under section 182(5)` `the answer under section 182(6)`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN     (   PARTY `ss 177-214 the director`
                 MUST `s 182(2)(a) the director declares at a meeting of the directors`
                 WITHIN (`s 182(4) the days allowed, counted from day 0` dayZero lastDay)
                 HENCE FULFILLED
                 LEST BREACH BY `ss 177-214 the director` BECAUSE "the director did not declare the interest as soon as was reasonably practicable (s 182(4)): a failure to comply with s 182, which is an offence under s 183(1)")
         ROR (   PARTY `ss 177-214 the director`
                 MUST `s 182(2)(b) the director declares by notice in writing`
                 WITHIN (`s 182(4) the days allowed, counted from day 0` dayZero lastDay)
                 HENCE FULFILLED
                 LEST BREACH BY `ss 177-214 the director` BECAUSE "the director did not declare the interest as soon as was reasonably practicable (s 182(4)): a failure to comply with s 182, which is an offence under s 183(1)")
         ROR (   PARTY `ss 177-214 the director`
                 MUST `s 182(2)(c) the director declares by general notice`
                 WITHIN (`s 182(4) the days allowed, counted from day 0` dayZero lastDay)
                 HENCE FULFILLED
                 LEST BREACH BY `ss 177-214 the director` BECAUSE "the director did not declare the interest as soon as was reasonably practicable (s 182(4)): a failure to comply with s 182, which is an offence under s 183(1)")
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:2413 | 182 Declaration of interest in existing transaction or arrangement
-- src:2414 | (1) Where a director of a company is in any way, directly or indirectly, interested in a transaction or arrangement that has been entered into by the company, he must declare the nature and extent of the interest to the other directors in accordance with this section.
-- src:2415 | This section does not apply if or to the extent that the interest has been declared under section 177 (duty to declare interest in proposed transaction or arrangement).
-- src:2416 | (2) The declaration must be made—
-- src:2417 | (a) at a meeting of the directors, or
-- src:2418 | (b) by notice in writing (see section 184), or
-- src:2419 | (c) by general notice (see section 185).
-- src:2422 | Failure to comply with this requirement does not affect the underlying duty to make the declaration.
@ref s 182(1), (2) and (4) The underlying duty survives a late declaration (src:2413-2419 and src:2422)
-- TIMELINE: unit=none; day 0=the day the director's duty to declare arises; counting=silent (s 182(4) says that failure to declare as soon as is reasonably practicable "does not affect the underlying duty to make the declaration", so no clock ends this duty: it stays owed until the declaration is made, however late)
GIVEN `the director is in any way, directly or indirectly, interested in a transaction or arrangement that has been entered into by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interest has been declared under section 177` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer under section 182(5)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under section 182(6)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ss 177-214 party` `ss 177-214 act`
`s 182(1) the director's underlying duty to declare, which a late declaration still discharges` MEANS
    IF (`s 182(1) the director is obliged to declare the nature and extent of the interest to the other directors` `the director is in any way, directly or indirectly, interested in a transaction or arrangement that has been entered into by the company` `the interest has been declared under section 177` `the answer under section 182(5)` `the answer under section 182(6)`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN     (PARTY `ss 177-214 the director` MUST `s 182(2)(a) the director declares at a meeting of the directors` HENCE FULFILLED)
         ROR (PARTY `ss 177-214 the director` MUST `s 182(2)(b) the director declares by notice in writing` HENCE FULFILLED)
         ROR (PARTY `ss 177-214 the director` MUST `s 182(2)(c) the director declares by general notice` HENCE FULFILLED)
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- ---- s 197: loans to directors, and the exceptions of ss 204 and 207 taken as gates ---------------------------------------------------

-- The exceptions as Boolean gates. s 204(1) and (2) answer JUST FALSE when the exception applies (approval "is not required") or is lost (over 50,000 pounds);
-- s 207(1) answers JUST TRUE when it applies. The helpers turn each into a plain yes or no.
-- src:2687 | 204 Exception for expenditure on company business
-- src:2688 | (1) Approval is not required under section 197, 198, 200 or 201 (requirement of members' approval for loans etc) for anything done by a company—
-- src:2689 | (a) to provide a director of the company or of its holding company, or a person connected with any such director, with funds to meet expenditure incurred or to be incurred by him—
-- src:2690 | (i) for the purposes of the company, or
-- src:2691 | (ii) for the purpose of enabling him properly to perform his duties as an officer of the company, or
-- src:2692 | (b) to enable any such person to avoid incurring such expenditure.
-- src:2693 | (2) This section does not authorise a company to enter into a transaction if the aggregate of—
-- src:2694 | (a) the value of the transaction in question, and
-- src:2695 | (b) the value of any other relevant transactions or arrangements,
-- src:2696 | exceeds £50,000.
@ref s 204 Exception for expenditure on company business (src:2687-2696)
-- FORK: s 204(2) "does not authorise ... if the aggregate ... exceeds 50,000 pounds" | the exception applies when s 204(1) says approval is not required and the aggregate does not exceed 50,000 pounds | the exception applies whenever s 204(1) says approval is not required
GIVEN `the thing done by the company is to provide a director of the company or of its holding company, or a person connected with any such director, with funds to meet expenditure incurred or to be incurred by him for the purposes of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing done by the company is to provide such a person with funds to meet expenditure incurred or to be incurred by him for the purpose of enabling him properly to perform his duties as an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing done by the company is to enable such a person to avoid incurring such expenditure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the transaction in question` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of any other relevant transactions or arrangements` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 204 the exception for expenditure on company business disapplies the requirement of approval` MEANS
        (`s 204(1) approval is required under section 197, 198, 200 or 201 for the thing done` `the thing done by the company is to provide a director of the company or of its holding company, or a person connected with any such director, with funds to meet expenditure incurred or to be incurred by him for the purposes of the company` `the thing done by the company is to provide such a person with funds to meet expenditure incurred or to be incurred by him for the purpose of enabling him properly to perform his duties as an officer of the company` `the thing done by the company is to enable such a person to avoid incurring such expenditure`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
    AND (NOT ((`s 204(2) section 204 authorises the company to enter into the transaction` `the value of the transaction in question` `the value of any other relevant transactions or arrangements`) EQUALS JUST FALSE))

-- src:2729 | 207 Exceptions for minor and business transactions
-- src:2730 | (1) Approval is not required under section 197, 198 or 200 for a company to make a loan or quasi-loan, or to give a guarantee or provide security in connection with a loan or quasi-loan, if the aggregate of—
-- src:2731 | (a) the value of the transaction, and
-- src:2732 | (b) the value of any other relevant transactions or arrangements,
-- src:2733 | does not exceed £10,000.
@ref s 207(1) Exception for a small loan: the aggregate does not exceed 10,000 pounds (src:2729-2733)
GIVEN transaction IS A `s 207 transaction`
      `the value of the transaction` IS A `s 211 value`
      `the value of any other relevant transactions or arrangements` IS A `s 211 value`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 207(1) the exception for a small loan disapplies the requirement of approval` MEANS
    (`s 207(1) approval under sections 197, 198 and 200 is not required by this section` transaction `the value of the transaction` `the value of any other relevant transactions or arrangements`) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- src:2570 | 197 Loans to directors: requirement of members' approval
-- src:2571 | (1) A company may not—
-- src:2572 | (a) make a loan to a director of the company or of its holding company, or
-- src:2573 | (b) give a guarantee or provide security in connection with a loan made by any person to such a director,
-- src:2574 | unless the transaction has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company.
-- src:2575 | (2) If the director is a director of the company's holding company, the transaction must also have been approved by a resolution of the members of the holding company.
@ref s 197(1) and (2) Loans to directors: requirement of members' approval (src:2570-2575)
-- TIMELINE: unit=none; day 0=not applicable; counting=silent (s 197(1) says the company "may not" make the loan unless approved and gives no time: the prohibition is open until the trace shows the company acting)
-- Gate: the bar of s 197(1) (with the exception answer the caller builds from the two helpers above and from ss 205, 206, 208 and 209) or the bar of s 197(2) for the members of the holding company.
-- FORK: s 197(2) "must also have been approved" | the answer under s 197(2) is an input and either bar makes the company's act a breach | s 197(2) is a separate rule
GIVEN `the company makes a loan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company gives a guarantee or provides security in connection with a loan made by any person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the borrower is a director of the company or of its holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 197(5) approval is required on the part of the members of the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `an exception in section 204, 205, 206, 207, 208 or 209 disapplies the requirement of approval` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer under section 197(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ss 177-214 party` `ss 177-214 act`
`s 197(1) the company's duty not to make or secure a loan to a director without the members' approval` MEANS
    IF     (`s 197(1) section 197(1) bars the company from the transaction` `the company makes a loan` `the company gives a guarantee or provides security in connection with a loan made by any person` `the borrower is a director of the company or of its holding company` `the transaction has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company` `s 197(5) approval is required on the part of the members of the company` `an exception in section 204, 205, 206, 207, 208 or 209 disapplies the requirement of approval`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
        OR (`the answer under section 197(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN PARTY `ss 177-214 the company`
         SHANT `s 197(1) the company makes the loan or gives the guarantee or provides the security`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `ss 177-214 the company` BECAUSE "the company made the loan to a director, or gave a guarantee or security for one, without the approval of a resolution of the members that s 197 requires: the transaction is voidable at the company's instance (s 213(2)) and the persons in s 213(4) are liable to account and to indemnify (s 213(3))"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:2576 | (3) A resolution approving a transaction to which this section applies must not be passed unless a memorandum setting out the matters mentioned in subsection (4) is made available to members—
-- src:2577 | (a) in the case of a written resolution, by being sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time at which the proposed resolution is sent or submitted to him;
-- src:2578 | (b) in the case of a resolution at a meeting, by being made available for inspection by members of the company both—
-- src:2579 | (i) at the company's registered office for not less than 15 days ending with the date of the meeting, and
-- src:2580 | (ii) at the meeting itself.
-- src:2581 | (4) The matters to be disclosed are—
-- src:2582 | (a) the nature of the transaction,
-- src:2583 | (b) the amount of the loan and the purpose for which it is required, and
-- src:2584 | (c) the extent of the company's liability under any transaction connected with the loan.
@ref s 197(3) and (4) The memorandum must be made available before the resolution is passed (src:2576-2584)
-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the first day on which the memorandum is available for inspection at the company's registered office (for a resolution at a meeting); counting="not less than 15 days ending with the date of the meeting" (counted inclusively, so a memorandum first available 14 days before the meeting has been available for 15 days ending with the meeting day; the existing function s 197(3) holds the count and is the gate)
-- The Act does not say who must not pass the resolution; the members, who pass it, are the party. The Act does not say the resolution is void if passed without the memorandum.
-- FORK: s 197(3) "must not be passed unless a memorandum ... is made available" | the prohibition is on the members, a breach is passing the resolution when the existing s 197(3) function answers JUST FALSE, and a resolution so passed still counts as an approval for the company's rule above (the Act states no other consequence) | a resolution passed without the memorandum is no approval
GIVEN way IS A `Way a resolution is passed`
      `the memorandum sets out the matters mentioned in subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the memorandum was sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time at which the proposed resolution was sent or submitted to him` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day on which the memorandum was available for inspection at the company's registered office` IS A DATE
      `the day of the meeting` IS A DATE
      `the memorandum was available for inspection at the meeting itself` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ss 177-214 party` `ss 177-214 act`
`s 197(3) the members' duty not to pass the resolution without the memorandum made available` MEANS
    IF (`s 197(3) the memorandum has been made available to members as the subsection requires` way `the memorandum sets out the matters mentioned in subsection (4)` `the memorandum was sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time at which the proposed resolution was sent or submitted to him` `the first day on which the memorandum was available for inspection at the company's registered office` `the day of the meeting` `the memorandum was available for inspection at the meeting itself`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN PARTY `ss 177-214 the members of the company`
         SHANT `s 197(3) the members pass the resolution approving the transaction`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `ss 177-214 the members of the company` BECAUSE "the resolution approving the loan was passed although the memorandum had not been made available to the members as s 197(3) requires"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- ---- s 213: the civil consequences of a loan made in contravention -----------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:2798 | (2) The transaction or arrangement is voidable at the instance of the company, unless—
-- src:2799 | (a) restitution of any money or other asset that was the subject matter of the transaction or arrangement is no longer possible,
-- src:2800 | (b) the company has been indemnified for any loss or damage resulting from the transaction or arrangement, or
-- src:2801 | (c) rights acquired in good faith, for value and without actual notice of the contravention by a person who is not a party to the transaction or arrangement would be affected by the avoidance.
@ref s 213(2) A transaction in contravention is voidable at the instance of the company (src:2798-2801)
-- TIMELINE: unit=none; day 0=the day the company enters into the transaction in contravention; counting=silent (s 213(2) gives the company no time in which to avoid it; the only limit is that s 214 ends the power on an affirmation "within a reasonable period", which enters here as an input and not as a clock)
-- Gate: s 213(2) with s 213(1) and the three limbs, and the answer under s 214 (a transaction affirmed "may no longer be avoided under section 213").
GIVEN `the answer under section 213(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `restitution of any money or other asset that was the subject matter is no longer possible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has been indemnified for any loss or damage resulting from the transaction or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `rights acquired in good faith, for value and without actual notice of the contravention by a person who is not a party would be affected by the avoidance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer under section 214` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ss 177-214 party` `ss 177-214 act`
`s 213(2) the company's power to avoid the transaction or arrangement` MEANS
    IF     (`s 213(2) the transaction or arrangement is voidable at the instance of the company` `the answer under section 213(1)` `restitution of any money or other asset that was the subject matter is no longer possible` `the company has been indemnified for any loss or damage resulting from the transaction or arrangement` `rights acquired in good faith, for value and without actual notice of the contravention by a person who is not a party would be affected by the avoidance`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND (NOT (`the answer under section 214` EQUALS JUST TRUE))
    THEN PARTY `ss 177-214 the company`
         MAY `s 213(2) the company avoids the transaction or arrangement`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:2802 | (3) Whether or not the transaction or arrangement has been avoided, each of the persons specified in subsection (4) is liable—
-- src:2803 | (a) to account to the company for any gain that he has made directly or indirectly by the transaction or arrangement, and
-- src:2804 | (b) (jointly and severally with any other person so liable under this section) to indemnify the company for any loss or damage resulting from the transaction or arrangement.
-- src:2810 | (5) Subsections (3) and (4) are subject to the following two subsections.
-- src:2811 | (6) In the case of a transaction or arrangement entered into by a company in contravention of section 200, 201 or 203 with a person connected with a director of the company or of its holding company, that director is not liable by virtue of subsection (4)(c) if he shows that he took all reasonable steps to secure the company's compliance with the section concerned.
-- src:2812 | (7) In any case—
-- src:2813 | (a) a person so connected is not liable by virtue of subsection (4)(b), and
-- src:2814 | (b) a director is not liable by virtue of subsection (4)(d),
-- src:2815 | if he shows that, at the time the transaction or arrangement was entered into, he did not know the relevant circumstances constituting the contravention.
@ref s 213(3) to (7) The persons liable account for any gain and indemnify the company (src:2802-2815)
-- TIMELINE: unit=none; day 0=the day the company enters into the transaction in contravention; counting="whether or not the transaction or arrangement has been avoided" (s 213(3) gives no time and says the liability does not depend on avoidance, so no clock runs and an affirmation under s 214 does not end it)
-- Both limbs are owed together (RAND); each is owed only where there is a gain, or a loss, to account or indemnify for. Joint and several liability (s 213(3)(b)) is not a time rule: each person liable owes the whole loss, and the amount is Boolean in coa5-loans-exceptions.l4.
-- FORK: s 213(3) "any gain" and "any loss or damage" | a limb is owed only where the trace states a gain or a loss | both limbs are owed whatever the amount (which may be nothing)
GIVEN `the answer under section 213(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under section 213(6)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under section 213(7)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person has made a gain directly or indirectly by the transaction or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has suffered loss or damage resulting from the transaction or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ss 177-214 party` `ss 177-214 act`
`s 213(3) the duty of each person liable to account for the gain and indemnify the company` MEANS
    IF (`s 213(3) the person is liable to account to the company for any gain and to indemnify it for any loss` `the answer under section 213(4)` `the answer under section 213(6)` `the answer under section 213(7)`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN     (IF `the person has made a gain directly or indirectly by the transaction or arrangement`
              THEN PARTY `ss 177-214 a person liable under section 213(4)`
                   MUST `s 213(3)(a) the person accounts to the company for the gain`
                   HENCE FULFILLED
              ELSE FULFILLED)
         RAND (IF `the company has suffered loss or damage resulting from the transaction or arrangement`
              THEN PARTY `ss 177-214 a person liable under section 213(4)`
                   MUST `s 213(3)(b) the person indemnifies the company for the loss or damage`
                   HENCE FULFILLED
              ELSE FULFILLED)
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- ---- s 214: affirmation ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- "Within a reasonable period" is a standard and not a number: the last day of the period is a judgment of the caller, counted from day 0 by the helper.
GIVEN dayZero IS A DATE
      lastDay IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 214 the days in a reasonable period, counted from day 0` MEANS
    IF (Day lastDay) AT LEAST (Day dayZero)
    THEN (Day lastDay) MINUS (Day dayZero)
    ELSE 0

-- src:2818 | Where a transaction or arrangement is entered into by a company in contravention of section 197, 198, 200, 201 or 203 (requirement of members' approval for loans etc) but, within a reasonable period, it is affirmed—
-- src:2819 | (a) in the case of a contravention of the requirement for a resolution of the members of the company, by a resolution of the members of the company, and
-- src:2820 | (b) in the case of a contravention of the requirement for a resolution of the members of the company's holding company, by a resolution of the members of the holding company,
-- src:2821 | the transaction or arrangement may no longer be avoided under section 213.
@ref s 214 Loans etc: effect of subsequent affirmation (src:2818-2821)
-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the company enters into the transaction in contravention; counting="within a reasonable period" (the Act gives no number: the last day is a date the caller supplies as a judgment, and an affirmation on that day is in time)
-- After the period lapses the power of affirmation under s 214 has no effect and nothing follows (LEST FULFILLED); the company's power to avoid under s 213(2) is its own rule above and stays open.
-- FORK: s 214 "within a reasonable period" | the members may affirm up to and including the caller's last day, and after it the affirmation no longer has the effect s 214 gives | the period is open-ended
-- FORK: s 214 "the members of the company" | one rule, for the resolution of the members of the company, where the contravention is of the requirement of a resolution of the company's members; the holding company's members (s 214(b)) are the same rule run again | a second rule for the holding company
GIVEN `the answer under section 213(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      dayZero IS A DATE
      lastDay IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ss 177-214 party` `ss 177-214 act`
`s 214 the members' power to affirm the transaction or arrangement` MEANS
    IF (`the answer under section 213(1)`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `ss 177-214 the members of the company`
         MAY `s 214 the members of the company affirm the transaction or arrangement by resolution`
         WITHIN (`s 214 the days in a reasonable period, counted from day 0` dayZero lastDay)
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED
